2023-12-21 - Hansard 21st December 2023.pdf", "source_url": "https://www.parliament.gh/epanel/docs/pb/21ST  DECEMBER 2023.pdf", "sha256_pdf": "0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce", "doc_id": "Hansard 21st December, 2023", "title": "Hansard 21st December, 2023"}}, {"rank": 5, "chunk_id": "1c928850191f5103fa171ff005ed6a6edbacfdd266532bdeb39a4b0eb83f73d3:36", "distance": 0.8771886825561523, "metadata": {"chunk_len_words": 512, "title": "Hansard 22nd December, 2023", "date_iso": "2023-12-22", "source_url": "https://www.parliament.gh/epanel/docs/pb/22 December  2023.pdf", "sha256_pdf": "1c928850191f5103fa171ff005ed6a6edbacfdd266532bdeb39a4b0eb83f73d3", "pdf_path": "data/corpus/clean/pdfs/2023-12-22 - Hansard 22nd December 2023.pdf", "chunk_index": 36, "doc_id": "Hansard 22nd December, 2023"}}]}, "prev_hash": "6a52dbcf7923e4967a7548627102d654ebda53c7aab00bd9228896e9d2d76a5e", "event_hash": "01b3fb6d5c277c5acebb8c0c7948627e08dddda09eae1d4ecc83b6406ec4a1de"}
{"ts_utc": "2026-05-12T16:05:26.402596Z", "run_id": "20260512_160410_rag_L3_B4_118009", "seq": 5, "event": "generation.completed", "payload": {"answer": "The budget, taxation, or public finance issues discussed in Parliament include:\n\n* The need for a thorough review of Parliament's budget during its mid-year review due to limited fiscal space [604cec5146650800cdce602f4fc1f04973f95b3be158e79c6d1f0ddde7da03e9:83].\n* The allocation of budgetary needs for various Committees, including the Public Accounts Committee and Committee on Government Assurance, which were found to be woefully inadequate [1c928850191f5103fa171ff005ed6a6edbacfdd266532bdeb39a4b0eb83f73d3:36].\n* The capping of capital expenditure, which has been reduced [604cec5146650800cdce602f4fc1f04973f95b3be158e79c6d1f0ddde7da03e9:83].\n* The need to boost the oversight responsibility of Parliament by reconsidering the criteria for allocating Committee sums [1c928850191f5103fa171ff005ed6a6edbacfdd266532bdeb39a4b0eb83f73d3:36].\n\nAdditionally, the following taxation-related issues were discussed:\n\n* The Customs (Amendment) Bill, 2023 [0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce:0].\n* The Value Added Tax (Amendment) Bill, 2023 [0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce:0].\n* The Excise Duty (Amendment) Bill, 2023 [0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce:0].\n* The Excise Stamp (Amendment) Bill, 2023 [0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce:0].\n* The Exemptions (Amendment) Bill, 2023 [0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce:0].\n* The Income Tax (Amendment) (No. 2) Bill, 2023 [0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce:0].\n* The Emissions Levy Bill, 2023 [0bfc34507981421ca2fb15dcadf24c621ed5885cdaa33c53f3e83214297d60ce:0].\n\nThe Loan Agreement between the Government of Ghana and Kreditanstalt fur Wiederaufbau (KfW) was also discussed [1c928850191f5103fa171ff005ed6a6edbacfdd266532bdeb39a4b0eb83f73d3:36].", "answer_sha256": "b0b8f0d827716a85ccc8a3489f173839b0c9328356bde76d8312f6b1a42db8db"}, "prev_hash": "01b3fb6d5c277c5acebb8c0c7948627e08dddda09eae1d4ecc83b6406ec4a1de", "event_hash": "3f9f8190508cf0eb0ffa79fd6c8e99aa8ecf3231e7ff5c9c6643e631efc9d0a8"}
